Flush each stamped line in ts.
When standard output was a pipe or a file, ts left its lines in the
stdio buffer until it filled or input ended, so in a live pipeline such
as "cmd | ts | tee log" lines showed up late and in bursts, long after
the times stamped on them. Flush after every line, as moreutils ts does.

---
 miscutils/ts.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/miscutils/ts.c
+++ b/miscutils/ts.c
@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@
 		} else {
 			printf("%s.%06u %s", date_buf, (unsigned)ts.tv_usec, line);
 		}
+		/* write each line out when it is stamped */
+		fflush_all();
 		free(line);
 	}
 
